div.p:
The work of Banerjee, Banerjee, Chowdhry and Thomas could also be seen as a kind of activism. These writers are united in their endeavor to unearth silences – be they the voices of those silenced (as in

 Recasting Women

), or the untold narrative (suppressed by the curator of the photography exhibit). The methodology of using non-archival sources (and I use this definition very loosely, for lack of a better one) has far-reaching theoretical implications. By using these sources, historians can simultaneously question authority and bestow it where it has formerly been denied. To borrow from Habermas, they are rethinking and reworking the public sphere.
